00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.820
ANDY CHANG: Hi, everyone.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.550
I'm Andy Chang, I'm a product
manager on Google's privacy

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:08.810
and security team.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.490
Really happy to be here today
to talk to you a little bit

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.860
about the lessons we've
learned from securing Google,

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:17.580
and from securing Google
customers on Google Cloud.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.580
So enterprises today are
seeing an increasing number

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.400
of breaches, and the increasing
number of breaches being

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.680
reported in an increasing
number of ways in a larger

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.070
scope in the public.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:32.049
And this trend does not
seem to be decreasing.

00:00:32.049 --> 00:00:36.450
On a very regular basis,
the increase in data,

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.840
that's sensitive data that's
being collected, created,

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:41.670
combined with the
attackers increased

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:43.620
